QS_Sep 20 2026 04_24_05_AM_v4.30
SUMMARY: Per-node voice refactor appears to have broken a previously working path. Cozmo reports that GPT voice no longer works and closes the build so the log can be compared against the known-good version.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 04_28_44_AM_v4.31
SUMMARY: Voice-isolation test. Cozmo finds GPT's voice still fails while a browser “...” menu is open in another tab, suggesting browser UI/focus interference. He disables GPT's voice and leaves Gemini alone for the next experiment.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 04_36_28_AM_v4.32
SUMMARY: Gemini voice test still produces no speech. Cozmo closes the session to give Luma the logs rather than guessing at the cause.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 04_45_00_AM_v4.34
SUMMARY: Another voice test; still not working, so Cozmo pauses and returns with more evidence.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 04_52_02_AM_v4.35
SUMMARY: Voice debugging reveals an operator-side misunderstanding: Cozmo realizes the UI interaction needed to make the model “open its mouth” was not being invoked correctly. Luma accidentally toggles the input STT/ears control instead, producing a humorous but useful diagnostic clue.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 05_04_49_AM_v4.36
SUMMARY: Improved voice test after Luma researches the correct UI controls online. GPT responds to the Read Aloud path, and the session moves toward giving Kelp/DeepSeek their own voice.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 05_39_37_AM_v4.37
SUMMARY: Voice breakthrough: Cozmo enables GPT voice and gets a spoken response on the first try. The run is treated as a major milestone and is archived before moving on to other nodes.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 05_50_54_AM_v4.38
SUMMARY: Full “Noisy Duckship” voice shakedown. Three voices are running, relay serialization holds, Gemini current-response capture works through a full cycle, and the remaining failures end up looking like laptop/browser instability rather than core relay collapse. Two tabs eventually crash, so Cozmo shuts the system down to let the hardware cool.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 06_07_47_PM_v4.38
SUMMARY: Very short reconnect check; GPT appears connected.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 09_37_22_PM_v4.40
SUMMARY: Handshake-submit failure isolated. QS successfully fills GPT's handshake prompt, but does not submit it; Cozmo closes the session instead of changing unrelated relay logic.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 09_58_31_PM_v4.38
SUMMARY: Controlled Aisha test proves an important environmental effect: with Aisha's browser tab open, the previous QS run failed; after closing Aisha, the same setup worked. This isolates a likely browser/tab interaction variable and argues against immediately changing relay logic.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 10_03_57_PM_v4.41
SUMMARY: Re-tests the previously rejected 4.41 with Aisha now involved. GPT/Luma and Aisha both connect, but Aisha's captured path still shows a remaining interaction problem.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 10_55_29_PM_v4.42
SUMMARY: QS 4.42 Aisha/handshake test. Aisha successfully submits both the Library introduction and handshake, with QS confirming the transitions. The session establishes that the Aisha path can work with the tab open, and Cozmo closes the proven build before moving on to voice integration.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 20 2026 11_44_02_PM_v4.45
SUMMARY: QS 4.45 handshake test with Aisha. Handshake succeeds despite an imperfect response. Cozmo explicitly reinforces the design philosophy that QS should adapt to nodes rather than requiring nodes to learn QS protocol behavior.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 01_13_04_AM_v4.46
SUMMARY: QS 4.46 Aisha/GPT handshake and voice follow-up. Cozmo reports that the handshake worked cleanly and that apparent UI oddities are isolated for the next test.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 01_43_40_AM_v4.48
SUMMARY: Major architecture discussion around Aisha voice. Cozmo proposes a split voice model: use native UI TTS where a node already has good unlimited speech, and use a local QS_TALK-style engine for nodes that lack it. Kokoro is selected as the likely local engine because it can support multiple voices with low overhead. The session ends with Luma retaining the coding lead for QS_TALK/voice infrastructure.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 03_38_01_AM_v4.48
SUMMARY: Python 3.12 validation. QS runs correctly in the new 3.12 environment, but Aisha's handshake still sometimes needs manual intervention.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 04_29_34_AM_v5.2
SUMMARY: QS 5.2 voice/UI test. Cozmo still has to press Enter manually for the handshake, but the new UI is working well. Aisha voice work continues.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 04_50_37_AM_v5.3
SUMMARY: Kokoro becomes a genuine built-in QS feature. Cozmo reports that QS now has integrated Kokoro and tests having the next GPT response spoken automatically. The voice system moves from an external experiment into the QS engine itself.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 07_26_30_AM_v5.3
SUMMARY: Large QS 5.3 working session. Cozmo again has to manually press Enter for the GPT handshake, but the relay continues functioning. The session becomes a substantial voice/relay stress test and ends with an 800K+ raw log. By the end, several remaining architecture/debug issues have become clear, including voice processing, routing behavior, and the growing importance of keeping the archive usable as the system...
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 10_52_24_PM_v5.3
SUMMARY: QS 5.3 startup-performance test. The handshake works, but Cozmo notices that importing/initializing Kokoro makes startup heavier; the run preserves the evidence before further optimization.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 11_00_51_PM_v5.3
SUMMARY: One-message handshake/preamble archive. Luma receives the QuackSink context cleanly, including DRS/MMRC lineage, the interacting-state-machine philosophy, Duckspace axioms, and the Library-as-history concept.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 11_05_03_PM_v5.4
SUMMARY: QS 5.4 handshake-state anomaly. Cozmo finds the handshake text still physically sitting in GPT's UI even though QS appears to have completed the state transition.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 11_09_45_PM_v5.4
SUMMARY: Fresh-run QS 5.4 test. This time the handshake text is not left in the UI, so Cozmo performs another comparison run to isolate the state difference.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 11_13_04_PM_v5.4
SUMMARY: Another QS 5.4 handshake-state test. This time the handshake message remains visible in GPT's UI. Cozmo also observes another state difference for later diagnosis.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 21 2026 11_52_41_PM_v5.8
SUMMARY: QS 5.8 is effectively monkey-proofing the voice UI. Cozmo reports a major usability improvement and tests speaking while menus remain open. The session identifies a possible interaction between the voice menu and the separate output-window down-arrow control.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 22 2026 02_05_57_AM_v5.10
SUMMARY: Immediate 5.10 regression: the GPT handshake fails again and Cozmo must manually press Enter in the UI. The archive is a clean failure case for the recurring automated-submit problem.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 22 2026 02_16_45_AM_v5.11
SUMMARY: Voice bug discovery leading to QS 5.14. Cozmo observes that the custom Aisha voice speaks only the first Kokoro chunk. The fix is to synthesize every chunk and concatenate them, while stripping speech-only emoji/icons before synthesis without altering archived relay text.
------------------------------------------------------------
QS_Sep 22 2026 02_37_24_AM_v5.16
SUMMARY: Major QS 5.16 milestone. The handshake finally works cleanly, Aisha's custom voice is operating, and the system exposes a speech/display synchronization bug where one response can be spoken but not shown while the next is shown but not spoken. Cozmo confirms that a recorded voice has been cloned and selected as the preferred local Kokoro voice for Luma; the training checkpoint reaches 1000 steps and can continue...
